     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Dear all, <div><br></div><div>I would like to have different colors within a category. I have the following code: </div><div><br></div><div>radioButtons(&quot;colors&quot;, label=&quot;colorcode&quot;, choices=list(&quot;red&quot;=1, &quot;orange&quot;=2, &quot;yellow&quot;=3, &quot;green&quot;=4, &quot;blue&quot;=5))</div><div><br></div><div>However, it would be awesome if the text could be transformed in the colors mentioned in the text, so that: </div><div>red will be <font color=\"#ff0000\">red</font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">orange will be </font><font color=\"#ff9900\">orange</font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">etcetera. </font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">Hopefully, you can help me! </font></div></div>"
    ]
